**Definitions section, GAP Waiver Addenda.** These definitions read the same under every plan, from GAP Waiver 120 through GAP Waiver Premier 150.

**Loss.** A loss under the addendum is one where the primary insurer declares the vehicle a total loss, or the vehicle is stolen and not recovered, and in either case the insurer pays its actual cash value.

**Primary insurance.** The borrower's own physical-damage insurance must have been in force on the date of loss. Force-placed coverage does not count as the borrower's own insurance.

**Contract status at loss.** A benefit is payable only when the contract's status on the date of loss was active.

**Claims per addendum.** At most 1 claim is decided on one addendum.

**Benefit balance.** The benefit starts from the contract principal balance on the date of loss as if every installment had been paid on its due date, plus interest accrued to the date of loss on that balance.

**Excluded amounts.** The benefit never covers:

- past-due installments;
- late charges and fees;
- installments deferred by extensions;
- refunds of cancellable add-on products;
- the primary deductible above the reimbursement;
- salvage value retained by the borrower;
- prior-damage deductions;
- capitalised collateral protection insurance premiums.

**Salvage retained.** When the borrower keeps the salvage, the amount excluded is the salvage value the primary insurer deducted from its settlement.

| Situation on the date of loss | Effect under these definitions |
|---|---|
| Borrower's own physical-damage policy in force | primary insurance requirement met |
| Only force-placed coverage in force | requirement not met |
| Contract active | status requirement met |
| Contract in any other status | status requirement not met |
